\f1\fs22 Alexander had no notion of Rotherhithe, nor the Gibson Desert, nor interest in any earthquake in the history of the world. Yet, as he sat fuming in a guest suite of the bunker\'97locked in by his own treacherous mother who had not the first inkling of how the entertainment industry worked\'97he thought he felt one. It was rather disappointing; it only lasted a few seconds, and nothing cracked or fell or sparked, but it was immediately followed by a 
\f2\i click
\f1\i0  from the locked door. \
